Package: ldfreq
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Lexical Diversity and Frequency Profiles
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Ryuya",
        family = "Komuro",
        email = "komuro.4121@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Computes explicitly versioned lexical-diversity metrics from
    ordered tokens and provides a separate auditable path from raw English text.
    Tokenization, Unicode normalization, case handling, lexical-unit selection,
    optional lemmatization and caller-supplied AntBNC flemma backends, and
    word-inclusion decisions remain visible in preprocessing provenance.
    Canonical long-form metric results retain
    method, parameter, schema, and contract identity in ordinary columns. A
    separate sensitivity surface exposes explicit Maas and sequential-MTLD
    formula variants. Coverage-aware lexical level profiles accept a
    caller-supplied New JACET 8000 list and report exact and cumulative token-
    and type-weighted rates without redistributing that resource. A byte-pinned
    TUBELEX aggregate supports a separately versioned frequency and prevalence
    profile while retaining resource identity and coverage.
